  <h2 id="parents">If you are a parent reading this chart</h2>

  <p>
    Your job is not to choose for your child. It is to improve the quality of the decision. Read the chart together, ask which door your child would hate to see closed, and compare the years and costs honestly.
  </p>

  <ul class="rich-list rich-list--plain">
    <li>Ask what your child can finish this month, not only which college name sounds safe.</li>
    <li>Compare years to work and total cost across two routes before comparing prestige.</li>
    <li>Never pay a fee before the institute's approval and the total fee are in writing.</li>
    <li>A modest route with real proof of skill is safer than an expensive route with none.</li>
  </ul>

